WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:08.967
- There are no players on the floor.

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:10.176
The clock hit zero.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.472
[Tape rewinding]

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:16.933
- [Pilot:] Welcome to Orlando.

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:19.310
The local time is 10:33.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:25.358
- The NBA playoffs have arrived!

00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:31.031
[players laughing]

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.323
- [Jae Crowder:] Thank you.

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:33.992
Appreciate it, man.

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:37.037
- ♪ And I can be ready ♪

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.830
They playing the jams.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.001
- [Jimmy Butler:] Goran don't got his mask on, NBA.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.963
- [Paul George:] Y'all late. Come on, Taylor.

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:48.131
- Next time I'll be on time.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.966
- Be on time.

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.510
- So luckily playoffs are underway,

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.554
and while the games are fun,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.306
there are a couple series

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.932
that look like they have the potential

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:00.560
to end up being some sweeps.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.520
Get out the brooms, folks.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.396
Alrighty.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.441
Headed to Sixers-Celtics,
Game 1 for them.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.320
- Hey, Jayson.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.363
We wish we were there
in the bubble with you

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:13.198
to support you,

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:16.409
but now that you have our
1,000 percent support from home,

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.078
one, two, three.

00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:21.122
- [Both:] Good luck!

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:25.210
[shoes squeaking]

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.922
[upbeat festive music]

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.216
[crowd cheering]

00:01:31.216 --> 00:01:32.467
- [Announcer:] Jaylen Brown!

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.053
- Gordon Hayward
went down with an injury

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:37.722
in Game 1 against the Sixers.

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:41.059
After the game, Brad Stevens
said it was a sprained ankle.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:42.268
- Sprained ankle.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.024
Don't know the severity,
but he's clearly in pain.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:50.777
And looked like it had
some swelling already.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.988
- But then we saw
Gordon walk out with crutches.

00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:57.742
[background chatting]

00:01:57.742 --> 00:01:58.827
Oh God, Gordon is hurt.

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:01.579
So fingers crossed it isn't too bad,

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:02.747
but doesn't look great.

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:06.918
[upbeat hip-hop music]

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:12.173
[crowd cheering]

00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:14.801
[buzzer beeping]

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.052
- [Announcer:] Final score:

00:02:16.052 --> 00:02:19.639
Philadelphia 76ers 106,
Boston Celtics 110.

00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:24.352
♪ Defense ♪

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:25.812
♪ Defense ♪

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.147
- [Taylor:] Woah!

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.068
- [Announcer:] Final score from today’s game:
Toronto 150, Brooklyn Nets 122.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:37.240
- One of the best things to do
at the end of these long days:

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.741
You see these heels?

00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:41.077
That's not gonna work as I get to the bus.

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:44.622
Pro tip: You always, always, always

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.041
have flats you don't care about

00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:47.917
that you can throw on.

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:49.752
[shoes thumping]

00:02:49.752 --> 00:02:51.921
Cuz we got a bus to catch.

00:02:51.921 --> 00:02:54.966
[crowd cheering]

00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:56.801
- [Announcer:] No shot.

00:02:57.927 --> 00:03:01.014
[ominous rock music]

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:07.520
- [Taylor:] Hey Jimmy.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.814
So you have been playing great basketball.

00:03:09.814 --> 00:03:11.149
You seem to be having fun out there.

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:12.400
You're winning.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.819
What is it about the
Miami Heat specifically

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.988
that has allowed you to
thrive at this level?

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:18.239
- I get to be me.

00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:21.326
I get to cuss people out when
they're not doing their job.

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:23.661
They're gonna cuss me out
whenever I'm not doing mine.

00:03:23.661 --> 00:03:25.121
I'm gonna take nothing personal.

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:26.706
It's on to the next play
because everybody knows

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:31.044
that whenever I say something, I mean well.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.295
May not come out the right way,

00:03:32.295 --> 00:03:35.131
but I mean well, and it goes
that way across the board.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:38.927
[crowd cheering]

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:41.179
- [Announcer:] Jimmy Butler!

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:46.476
- There are so many
games, so many practices

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:47.852
happening every single day,

00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:49.395
but we are still in the midst

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.482
of some competitive playoff series.

00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:57.487
We've got Bucks-Magic, who
need to continue their games.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:01.157
There's Lakers-Blazers, Rockets-Thunder,

00:04:01.157 --> 00:04:04.202
Jazz-Nuggets, Clippers-Mavericks.

00:04:04.202 --> 00:04:06.204
Yeah, those are the ones that are left.

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.623
So still some series left.

00:04:08.623 --> 00:04:10.291
Still teams fighting for a win,

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:12.919
trying to make it to the second round.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.338
So expect some big finishes.

00:04:15.338 --> 00:04:16.714
- [Interviewer:] How do you get the squad

00:04:16.714 --> 00:04:18.383
to meet that standard

00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:21.594
of, you know, day one—of course you’ve all
been there a million times.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.013
So how does that play out to this?

00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:25.765
- I'm not smiling at your question.

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:28.476
Anthony is behind where you guys settin’ stuff up, man.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:35.984
Y'all, I'm gonna call you, Anthony.

00:04:35.984 --> 00:04:37.026
I'll meet you in your room.
- No, the Browns about

00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:38.945
to play in the Super Bowl, so yeah.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:42.282
- Oh, OK. I'll see you in a little bit.

00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:45.827
[crowd cheering]

00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:49.080
[upbeat hip-hop music]

00:04:50.581 --> 00:04:52.292
- [Announcer:] Three-ball,

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.584
Anthony Davis.

00:04:53.584 --> 00:04:55.837
- Game over, Lakers win.

00:04:55.837 --> 00:04:58.089
All right, I only have one game today.

00:04:58.089 --> 00:05:00.466
Lakers-Blazers, Game 3.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.843
Series is split.

00:05:03.344 --> 00:05:04.679
Who's winning it?

00:05:04.679 --> 00:05:05.847
Who's winning it today?

00:05:07.098 --> 00:05:10.351
[upbeat hip-hop music]

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.981
[crowd cheering]

00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:18.318
[upbeat rhythmic music]

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.944
- [Announcer:] Basket, Davis.

00:05:19.944 --> 00:05:22.155
- So the officiating
in the bubble so far

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:23.906
has been a little shaky.

00:05:23.906 --> 00:05:25.950
It feels like they're
calling technicals on things

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.618
that wouldn't normally be techs.

00:05:27.618 --> 00:05:28.828
Lot of foul calls.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.788
I wonder how much the lack of a crowd

00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:33.416
has to do with that, but
it hasn't been the best.

00:05:34.459 --> 00:05:37.837
[upbeat rhythmic music]

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.505
- [Announcer:] Three!

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:42.300
[crowd cheering]

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.218
- Mavs vs. Clippers.

00:05:44.218 --> 00:05:47.305
Porzingis got
ejected and it was weak.

00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:49.265
Weak call, weak sauce.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.770
[background chatting]

00:05:55.897 --> 00:05:58.149
[muffled speaking]

00:05:58.149 --> 00:05:59.984
You know, when it comes to playoff time,

00:05:59.984 --> 00:06:01.694
every single thing counts, right?

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.654
And if you aren’t in the game,
people are thinking about,

00:06:03.654 --> 00:06:05.114
"OK, maybe the outcome was different

00:06:05.114 --> 00:06:06.574
if Kristaps was in the game."

00:06:06.574 --> 00:06:08.326
How do you get over that,

00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:10.495
thinking about maybe
what your absence did?

00:06:12.747 --> 00:06:14.582
- There's really not much
to do there, you know?

00:06:14.582 --> 00:06:17.293
You can think about the possibilities,

00:06:17.293 --> 00:06:20.046
but it is what is at this point.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.798
We're already past this game,

00:06:21.798 --> 00:06:24.217
and we're gonna look
at the mistakes we made

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:27.178
and things we could do
better for the second game.

00:06:27.178 --> 00:06:30.848
And our belief is still strong
that we can beat these guys.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.103
And that's it.

00:06:35.103 --> 00:06:37.271
If we didn’t have that belief,
we shouldn’t be here anyway.

00:06:37.271 --> 00:06:40.358
So that's our mindset
going into the second game.

00:06:40.358 --> 00:06:43.653
- This is the face of a very sad person.

00:06:43.653 --> 00:06:47.657
I'm sad because yesterday
I missed the overtime game

00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:49.867
between the Rockets and the Thunder.

00:06:49.867 --> 00:06:53.413
Then today I miss a monster
performance by Luka,

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:56.916
and an OT win from the
Mavericks beating the Clippers

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.252
and tying up the series,

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:02.380
because I didn't submit for that game!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.798
I missed it!

00:07:03.798 --> 00:07:05.842
Probably the best game of the bubble.

00:07:07.468 --> 00:07:10.179
[crowd cheering]

00:07:12.014 --> 00:07:13.891
[sneakers squeaking]

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:16.060
[buzzer squealing]

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.813
[crowd cheering]

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:20.773
Hey, Don.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:21.607
So obviously last game

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:24.110
you had 57
points, today you had 30.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.821
How have you almost become a chameleon?

00:07:26.821 --> 00:07:29.323
You can always adapt to
what the team needs from you

00:07:29.323 --> 00:07:30.950
at any given moment or any given game.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.869
How have you been able to do that?

00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:33.703
- I think the biggest thing for me

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:34.871
is just trying to, like you said,

00:07:34.871 --> 00:07:36.706
just reading the situation.

00:07:36.706 --> 00:07:38.416
I think, I said it earlier,

00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:42.670
my first two years I kinda saw
the rim and being a scorer.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.173
Now it's kinda, I prided
myself over quarantine to just how to become a playmaker.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.092
Find a way to get the team involved,

00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:51.137
and it may not always be scoring.

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:53.222
And I think today just
really trusting my teammates,

00:07:53.222 --> 00:07:54.974
and they did a hell of a job.

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:58.102
I mean Rudy [Gobert], Joe [Ingles],
J.C. [Jordan Clarkson], Royce [O’Neal], everybody,

00:07:58.102 --> 00:07:59.896
to be able to not just hit shots,

00:07:59.896 --> 00:08:01.314
but be ready and make plays.

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.316
I think that's what made it easy for me.

00:08:04.275 --> 00:08:07.528
- OK, I'm here
at Jazz vs. Nuggets.

00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:09.489
When I had Rudy Gobert on my show one year,

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:12.658
he was talking about how
people don't pay attention

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.661
to the team as much as they
should because it's in Utah.

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:16.913
And he's kinda right.

00:08:17.872 --> 00:08:20.583
Media is usually full at these games.

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:24.712
It's really just me and Rena hanging out.

00:08:24.712 --> 00:08:26.964
Shai, I stayed all this
time just to get a close-up

00:08:26.964 --> 00:08:28.341
of your hair.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:29.217
- Oh, wow.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:30.259
[Taylor laughing]

00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:32.386
You are dedicated.

00:08:32.386 --> 00:08:34.138
- [Reporter:] In the hands of Gallinari.

00:08:34.138 --> 00:08:35.139
How much do you attribute—

00:08:35.139 --> 00:08:35.973
[machine beeping]

00:08:35.973 --> 00:08:37.725
- [P.J. Tucker:] Hey, Russ [Westbrook], I can't
hear over here, thanks.

00:08:37.725 --> 00:08:38.726
I can't hear.

00:08:38.726 --> 00:08:39.560
I'm doing interviews, thank you.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:40.394
- All right, guess what?

00:08:40.394 --> 00:08:41.604
You know what they can't put on TV?

00:08:41.604 --> 00:08:44.023
I don't...no, but you know
it's too many cameras.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.526
[all laughing]

00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:49.237
[muffled speaking]

00:08:49.237 --> 00:08:51.405
- [Taylor:] What's the story?

00:08:51.405 --> 00:08:53.324
- You got a wire on?

00:08:53.324 --> 00:08:54.659
Oh, a wire, man.

00:08:54.659 --> 00:08:55.493
[Taylor laughing]

00:08:55.493 --> 00:08:58.329
- Only in the bubble, man.
- Only in the bubble.

00:09:00.748 --> 00:09:03.668
- [Announcer:] Three-point basket, James Harden.

00:09:04.669 --> 00:09:06.045
- Sitting here
waiting for the Lakers-

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.380
Blazers to start.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.883
Right now the Thunder-
Rockets game is in OT.

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:11.968
The Thunder are up.

00:09:11.968 --> 00:09:15.763
The Rockets haven't scored
once in all of overtime.

00:09:15.763 --> 00:09:18.599
I am sick that I'm missing it.

00:09:18.599 --> 00:09:21.936
[rhythmic upbeat music]

00:09:24.772 --> 00:09:27.400
[Announcer:] Dennis Schroder!

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.568
- OK, during our game break,

00:09:28.568 --> 00:09:29.443
eating food,

00:09:29.443 --> 00:09:31.487
but the Magic are playing the Bucks.

00:09:31.487 --> 00:09:34.115
They're up like 20 points,

00:09:34.115 --> 00:09:37.326
so I think everybody might
have overreacted after Game 1.

00:09:37.326 --> 00:09:39.453
The Raptors just swept the Nets,

00:09:39.453 --> 00:09:42.123
advancing to the second round.

00:09:42.123 --> 00:09:45.084
But Fred VanVleet didn't
want any basketball questions

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:47.044
asked at his press conference.

00:09:47.044 --> 00:09:48.796
He only wanted to talk about Jacob Blake,

00:09:48.796 --> 00:09:51.507
who was shot by the police
in the back multiple times.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:56.262
He was incredibly thoughtful,
visibly emotional,

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:57.471
had some tears in his eyes,

00:09:57.471 --> 00:09:59.807
but he is another example of players

00:09:59.807 --> 00:10:02.935
trying to say, you know, even
though we are in the playoffs,

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:05.271
there are other things
happening in the world

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:07.148
that are more important.

00:10:07.148 --> 00:10:08.482
[Taylor:] Hey, Fred.

00:10:08.482 --> 00:10:10.943
So I know that pulling up your phone

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:12.320
and seeing people that look like you

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.280
being killed by the police can be a lot.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:17.283
So I guess my question
is just how are you?

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:19.118
How are you doing mentally?

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:21.954
- I'm a little bit all over the place.

00:10:21.954 --> 00:10:26.042
Like I said, you start to
feel guilty a little bit.

00:10:27.501 --> 00:10:30.504
There's a lot of stuff
going on for me back home.

00:10:30.504 --> 00:10:31.797
People in my own community

00:10:32.882 --> 00:10:34.383
dying out by the hands of police,

00:10:34.383 --> 00:10:36.469
but it's just a byproduct of their environment.

00:10:37.928 --> 00:10:38.763
So you try to take all
that in, and we're here

00:10:38.763 --> 00:10:39.680
and we're isolated.

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:42.350
My family got to town yesterday.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.851
I don't get to see them for another week.

00:10:43.851 --> 00:10:48.731
So it'll be nice to hug and
kiss on my kids a little bit.

00:10:48.731 --> 00:10:50.441
But yeah, you just try to deal with it,

00:10:50.441 --> 00:10:52.276
and it's a lot to take in.

00:10:52.276 --> 00:10:56.530
I think we can't underestimate the trauma

00:10:56.530 --> 00:11:00.076
that we take in on a daily
basis from our phones

00:11:00.076 --> 00:11:01.285
and watching these videos.

00:11:01.285 --> 00:11:05.456
And you watch a guy get shot

00:11:05.456 --> 00:11:07.333
in front of his entire family,

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:10.002
and then right underneath that video

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:10.878
is somebody saying,

00:11:10.878 --> 00:11:12.963
"Hey, well he shoulda just
listened to the police."

00:11:12.963 --> 00:11:15.299
So you take all that in.

00:11:15.299 --> 00:11:16.592
Whether you register it or not.

00:11:16.592 --> 00:11:19.220
Whether you realize what
you're looking at or not.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.431
You're taking that in and
that depreciation of life,

00:11:22.431 --> 00:11:26.769
and you get numb to
what you're looking at.

00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:28.646
And you almost start to question yourself,

00:11:28.646 --> 00:11:30.856
like, “damn, maybe he shoulda listened,”

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:33.776
and you start to think, and
then you snap back to reality.

00:11:33.776 --> 00:11:35.403
Like, nah, that's not right.

00:11:35.403 --> 00:11:37.488
So it's a lot of emotions to take in.

00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:39.407
You just try to stay levelheaded

00:11:39.407 --> 00:11:43.285
and bounce ideas off of—
we got a tight group here.

00:11:43.285 --> 00:11:46.497
So like I said, we had a
chance to speak this morning,

00:11:46.497 --> 00:11:51.127
and however you see fit
to get that out, you do.

00:11:51.127 --> 00:11:53.254
But it's a lot, and we're
in the middle of it.

00:11:53.254 --> 00:11:54.714
I mean it's fresh.

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:56.257
It's fresh, but every time it's fresh

00:11:56.257 --> 00:11:58.926
it brings back old
stuff and reopens wounds,

00:11:58.926 --> 00:12:01.429
and my father was killed when I was young.

00:12:01.429 --> 00:12:05.266
So it's just a lot of things that go into

00:12:06.851 --> 00:12:08.769
taking all of this information in.

00:12:35.045 --> 00:12:36.380
- [Taylor:] There are no
players on the floor.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.506
The clock hit zero.

00:12:37.506 --> 00:12:39.175
The players came out and warmed up

00:12:39.175 --> 00:12:41.761
but went back, and it
seems like the chatter

00:12:41.761 --> 00:12:44.597
is there will be no Game 5 today.

00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:04.241
All games have been postponed.

00:13:07.244 --> 00:13:10.414
[background chatting]

00:13:14.084 --> 00:13:16.462
- Our focus today cannot be on basketball.

00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:18.964
- We are calling for
justice for Jacob Blake

00:13:18.964 --> 00:13:21.425
and demand the officers
be held accountable.

00:13:21.425 --> 00:13:22.968
- OK, August 27,

00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:26.222
a day after the NBA postponed their games

00:13:26.222 --> 00:13:29.892
as players sat out in
support of racial equality

00:13:29.892 --> 00:13:30.935
and social justice.

00:13:30.935 --> 00:13:32.812
I just got off the phone with some people,

00:13:32.812 --> 00:13:35.648
and what I am hearing about the joint call

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.608
between the owners and players

00:13:37.608 --> 00:13:40.611
is that it was incredibly productive.

00:13:40.611 --> 00:13:42.363
The main point was players stressed

00:13:42.363 --> 00:13:44.657
that they wanted there to
be a dedicated coalition

00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:46.116
that worked within the NBA

00:13:46.116 --> 00:13:51.121
whose full-time job was
to support certain causes

00:13:52.915 --> 00:13:55.543
on a grassroots level, local activists,

00:13:55.543 --> 00:13:58.254
funding them, supporting
them, amplifying their voice.

00:13:58.254 --> 00:14:00.714
A full-time coalition dedicated to that.

00:14:00.714 --> 00:14:02.758
I hear LeBron James was
the last player to speak

00:14:02.758 --> 00:14:04.009
on that call, and he stressed

00:14:04.009 --> 00:14:06.345
to the owners this has to be something

00:14:06.345 --> 00:14:09.056
that they care about
past the basketball season.

00:14:09.056 --> 00:14:10.766
Michael Jordan was also on that call

00:14:10.766 --> 00:14:14.645
and was an incredibly
strong voice as well.

00:14:14.645 --> 00:14:16.981
Friday, August 28.

00:14:16.981 --> 00:14:20.109
This is the first day of practices

00:14:20.109 --> 00:14:21.902
since the players decided to strike

00:14:21.902 --> 00:14:25.197
and not play these dates
of basketball games.

00:14:25.197 --> 00:14:27.867
I am headed to the Clippers practice.

00:14:27.867 --> 00:14:27.908
I am headed to the Clippers practice.

00:14:27.908 --> 00:14:29.159
[Taylor:] Hey, Doc.

00:14:29.159 --> 00:14:30.452
So we talk a lot about perspective,

00:14:30.452 --> 00:14:33.539
but in years to come when
history tells the story

00:14:33.539 --> 00:14:35.249
about these past couple days,

00:14:35.249 --> 00:14:37.543
what story do you want it to tell?

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:39.879
- Oh, man. Taylor, that’s too deep.

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:40.754
[all laughing]

00:14:40.754 --> 00:14:41.589
God.

00:14:42.923 --> 00:14:46.176
I want them to tell the story

00:14:46.176 --> 00:14:48.429
about what they're speaking about now,

00:14:49.305 --> 00:14:51.056
that the league is doing something.

00:14:51.056 --> 00:14:52.600
Whenever that story is told,

00:14:53.726 --> 00:14:56.103
they're talking about what's
happening at that moment,

00:14:56.103 --> 00:14:58.147
that it started then.

00:14:58.147 --> 00:15:00.774
The reason I say that, that means
they're still doing it.

00:15:02.192 --> 00:15:07.197
And this, I'm just hoping is
not a one-hit wonder thing.

00:15:07.823 --> 00:15:09.950
This has to continue.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:13.537
And I think that's why the
coalition is so important,

00:15:13.537 --> 00:15:14.622
because this is not about

00:15:14.622 --> 00:15:17.541
just today. Something's
gonna happen next week,

00:15:17.541 --> 00:15:18.375
next month.

00:15:19.376 --> 00:15:22.046
And we have to have a group in place

00:15:22.046 --> 00:15:23.547
to understand how to handle that,

00:15:23.547 --> 00:15:26.425
and understand how to help
the players process through it.

00:15:28.177 --> 00:15:31.096
And we have to have a group that

00:15:31.096 --> 00:15:34.516
is working on legislation all the time.

00:15:34.516 --> 00:15:38.812
Not just U.S., but state-
to-state legislation.

00:15:38.812 --> 00:15:43.817
And so I think that's the
story that I want told.

00:15:44.318 --> 00:15:45.152
- [Taylor:] Thank you.

00:15:45.152 --> 00:15:46.987
- Thanks, guys.
- Thank you.

00:15:46.987 --> 00:15:48.614
- [Doc:] Thanks for the deep
question, appreciate it.

00:15:48.614 --> 00:15:49.907
- For sure.
- No problem.

00:15:49.907 --> 00:15:50.282
- For sure.
- No problem.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:53.285
- The past couple days is a
change for the greater good

00:15:53.285 --> 00:15:54.119
of the future.

00:15:55.162 --> 00:15:57.081
When you see change
happening in the future

00:15:57.081 --> 00:15:58.624
and you can look back and say,

00:15:58.624 --> 00:16:01.168
"That was the moment when it happened,

00:16:01.168 --> 00:16:04.004
and that was a key
moment when it happened.”

00:16:05.506 --> 00:16:08.926
Obviously the bubble season
would never be forgotten

00:16:08.926 --> 00:16:09.885
when it comes to sports.

00:16:09.885 --> 00:16:11.512
This is the first time we've been able

00:16:11.512 --> 00:16:12.805
to do something like this.

00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:15.182
But obviously this
moment is so much bigger

00:16:15.182 --> 00:16:16.266
than us playing basketball.

00:16:16.266 --> 00:16:20.479
So hopefully the initiatives
that we came together

00:16:20.479 --> 00:16:21.605
that we partnered with—

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.567
voting and the sites and the arenas

00:16:25.567 --> 00:16:27.653
and things of that nature—

00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:29.446
hopefully years on down the line

00:16:29.446 --> 00:16:31.240
America is in a better place

00:16:32.533 --> 00:16:34.034
that you could look back to this moment

00:16:34.034 --> 00:16:36.328
and be like, “That was one of the catapults

00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:37.663
that got it going.”

00:16:38.831 --> 00:16:41.208
- Wanna shed some light
on what NBA coaches

00:16:41.208 --> 00:16:43.961
are doing to help this movement.

00:16:43.961 --> 00:16:48.257
They are playing such a big
role in amplifying the voices

00:16:48.257 --> 00:16:49.550
of the voiceless.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.677
I was just on the phone with
Atlanta Hawks head coach

00:16:51.677 --> 00:16:54.179
Lloyd Pierce, and he
was actually in the car

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:57.224
waiting for a call from
Jacob Blake Sr.,

00:16:57.224 --> 00:16:59.226
trying to figure out what they can do

00:16:59.226 --> 00:17:01.395
to help the situation.

00:17:01.395 --> 00:17:04.148
I also recently learned
that Mavs head coach

00:17:04.148 --> 00:17:06.108
Rick Carlisle played a pivotal role

00:17:06.108 --> 00:17:07.943
in some policy change in Dallas.

00:17:07.943 --> 00:17:10.821
He worked alongside local activists.

00:17:10.821 --> 00:17:14.116
August 29, the games
are starting back up.

00:17:17.327 --> 00:17:19.413
- [Announcer:] Giannis Antetokounmpo!

00:17:19.413 --> 00:17:21.790
[Crowd cheering]

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:25.711
[Upbeat hip-hop music]

00:17:25.711 --> 00:17:27.379
- [Announcer:] Three!

00:17:29.173 --> 00:17:30.924
[Whistle blowing]

00:17:30.924 --> 00:17:33.677
[Crowd cheering]

00:17:42.019 --> 00:17:43.062
- [Boban Marjanovic:] Hello, how are you?
- Good to see you.

00:17:43.062 --> 00:17:44.354
- Good to see you too.
- Yes.

00:17:44.354 --> 00:17:47.858
Oh my gosh, your fist is
so much bigger than mine.

00:17:47.858 --> 00:17:49.026
- It's working.
It’s going up.

00:17:49.026 --> 00:17:51.945
[Crowd:] Defense! Defense!

00:17:55.699 --> 00:17:57.284
[Crowd cheering]

00:17:57.284 --> 00:17:59.578
[Announcer:] Three-point basket, Jamal Murray.

00:17:59.578 --> 00:18:02.831
[Upbeat hip-hop music]

00:18:09.546 --> 00:18:11.840
- [Announcer:] Three more from the wing!

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:12.674
Luguentz Dort!

00:18:14.051 --> 00:18:15.052
- [Chris Paul:] Yes, sir.

00:18:15.052 --> 00:18:17.054
We just want a chance.

00:18:17.054 --> 00:18:18.889
We just wanted a chance.

00:18:18.889 --> 00:18:21.558
Yeah, Tim, we just want a chance!

00:18:21.558 --> 00:18:23.977
Yeah, Gallo.

00:18:23.977 --> 00:18:26.146
We just gave ourselves a chance.

00:18:26.146 --> 00:18:27.981
Game 7, anything can happen!

00:18:27.981 --> 00:18:30.526
- [Clapping]

00:18:31.735 --> 00:18:33.362
- [Taylor:] I mean, hearing that coming from you,

00:18:33.362 --> 00:18:35.739
how much does, like, that simple line fuel you?

00:18:35.739 --> 00:18:38.700
- It's just, you know, you down 3-2,

00:18:39.701 --> 00:18:41.954
and like I said, you come
into the bubble, it’s different.

00:18:41.954 --> 00:18:42.913
You gotta be packed,

00:18:42.913 --> 00:18:45.332
cuz the game at 9:00.

00:18:45.332 --> 00:18:48.752
You don't win the game, we
goin’ to the airport tomorrow.

00:18:48.752 --> 00:18:49.753
You know what I mean?

00:18:49.753 --> 00:18:51.505
So we gave ourselves a chance.

00:18:51.505 --> 00:18:52.339
That's all you want.

00:18:52.339 --> 00:18:53.173
Now it's 3-3.

00:18:53.173 --> 00:18:54.341
[Crowd cheering]

00:18:54.341 --> 00:18:56.802
- I don't feel good
about this for the Jazz.

00:18:56.802 --> 00:18:59.555
[Crowd cheering]

00:19:01.014 --> 00:19:03.600
[Whistle blowing]

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.477
- [Crowd:] Defense!

00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:07.437
Defense!

00:19:07.437 --> 00:19:09.648
Defense!

00:19:09.648 --> 00:19:12.568
Defense!

00:19:12.568 --> 00:19:14.862
Defense!

00:19:14.862 --> 00:19:17.614
[Crowd cheering]

00:19:22.953 --> 00:19:24.788
Defense!

00:19:24.788 --> 00:19:26.874
[Crowd groaning]

00:19:26.874 --> 00:19:29.877
[Announcer:] Ahhh!

00:19:31.044 --> 00:19:34.965
Final score:
Utah 78, Nuggets 80.

00:19:38.802 --> 00:19:39.636
Let's gooo!

00:19:41.597 --> 00:19:44.558
[Crowd cheering]

00:19:44.558 --> 00:19:47.811
[Upbeat hip-hop music]

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:01.074
- [Announcer:] Round 2, ding!

00:20:06.622 --> 00:20:07.664
- [Taylor:] Hey, Donovan.

00:20:07.664 --> 00:20:09.875
I know you've walked us
through the final play,

00:20:09.875 --> 00:20:11.376
what it was like through your head then.

00:20:11.376 --> 00:20:13.420
But once that was over,
you were on the floor

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:14.838
for a bit.

00:20:14.838 --> 00:20:15.839
Can you walk me through the emotions

00:20:15.839 --> 00:20:17.216
that you felt on the ground?

00:20:18.592 --> 00:20:22.221
- To be honest with you I'm in shock.

00:20:22.221 --> 00:20:24.056
That was really it.

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:26.516
I think the biggest
thing is we worked so hard

00:20:26.516 --> 00:20:29.102
as a unit, as a whole to get to a point

00:20:29.102 --> 00:20:32.231
that we got to, and we were
this close, you know?

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:36.485
We were down and came back and fought

00:20:37.527 --> 00:20:40.364
and fought and clawed,
and to be that close,

00:20:41.698 --> 00:20:42.574
that hurts.

00:20:42.574 --> 00:20:45.911
And I really didn't know what else to do.

00:20:45.911 --> 00:20:46.787
I was exhausted.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:50.249
I just kinda just laid there.

00:20:52.292 --> 00:20:54.211
I don't know, man. I just—

00:20:55.671 --> 00:20:56.797
that shit sucks.

00:20:58.757 --> 00:21:00.008
This is gonna be in my
mind for a long time.

00:21:00.008 --> 00:21:04.096
This kinda reminds me of last year

00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:05.847
being 4-of-23 from the field.

00:21:05.847 --> 00:21:08.183
That kinda fueled my entire season,

00:21:08.183 --> 00:21:09.601
Game 5 against Houston,

00:21:09.601 --> 00:21:12.437
and fueled everything I did this year.

00:21:14.022 --> 00:21:17.067
It's just another thing
to fuel for next year.

00:21:18.193 --> 00:21:19.778
I'll be back. We'll be back.

00:21:22.155 --> 00:21:24.700
But that's really what that was.

00:21:27.536 --> 00:21:30.289
[Crowd cheering]

00:21:33.375 --> 00:21:36.712
[Rhythmic upbeat music]

00:21:37.713 --> 00:21:40.215
[Whistle blowing]

00:21:40.215 --> 00:21:42.259
- OKC ball.

00:21:42.259 --> 00:21:45.012
1.1 seconds left.

00:21:46.596 --> 00:21:48.890
The anxiety! This is enough time.

00:21:49.808 --> 00:21:51.101
Catch and shoot, get a three.

00:21:54.104 --> 00:21:55.772
- [Crowd:] Defense!

00:21:55.772 --> 00:21:57.899
Defense!

00:21:57.899 --> 00:21:59.651
Defense!

00:21:59.651 --> 00:22:01.153
[Whistle blowing]

00:22:01.153 --> 00:22:03.280
[Crowd cheering]

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.782
- [Announcer:] Rockets win!

00:22:08.076 --> 00:22:11.038
- Round 1
was incredibly eventful,

00:22:11.038 --> 00:22:11.913
to say the least.

00:22:11.913 --> 00:22:13.373
We started off watching some players

00:22:13.373 --> 00:22:15.083
play very competitive basketball.

00:22:15.083 --> 00:22:16.001
Then there was a pause

00:22:16.001 --> 00:22:18.337
because players wanted to use their voice,

00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:20.088
protest against police brutality

00:22:20.088 --> 00:22:22.341
and racism that happens in this country.

00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:24.968
But now Round 1's over.

00:22:24.968 --> 00:22:27.179
Round 2 is set.

00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:28.347
And we'll see you then.

